msgid "The examples on this page call them through their default aliases (`@model`, `@env_detect`). `moonbitlang/async` is needed because `detect` is `async`: call it from an `async fn main` or an `async test`, like `runner.run`. The package builds on every target; `detect` runs where `moonbitlang/async` has a runtime (native, JS, wasm), and `new_run_id` is an ordinary function that runs everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/env_detect.md:39
msgid "Detection"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/env_detect.md:43
msgid "`detect` builds the environment snapshot of the running process."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/env_detect.md:49
msgid "Every argument is optional and named after the snapshot field it sets. A field passed as an argument is used as it is: it is not probed and never appears in `undetected`. For every other field `detect` does the following."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/env_detect.md:53
#: manual/api/fixture.md:46
#: manual/api/ir_model.md:292
#: manual/api/model.md:201
#: manual/api/runner.md:320
#: manual/api/stats.md:51
#: manual/api/stats.md:163
