#: manual/api/report.md:5
msgid "`Luna-Flow/mare_mark/report` turns a JSONL event stream into a Plot IR document and renders that document as `mmks_2` JSON, standalone SVG, a self-contained HTML page or a plain-text table. On the way it compares every implementation with a baseline, block by block, and decides with the threshold and outlier policy the run recorded. All five functions are pure: they take strings and values and return strings. Reading and writing files is the job of the [`cli`](cli.md). The projection and the comparison rules are derived in the [report design](../design/report.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:14
msgid "Source: [`src/report/report.mbt`](../../../src/report/report.mbt)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:27
msgid "The examples on this page call them through their default aliases (`@ir_model`, `@report`)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:30
msgid "Parsing events"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:34
msgid "`document_from_jsonl` parses a JSONL event stream into a `PlotDocument`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:40
msgid "`target` (default `\"unknown\"`) is copied into the document; the events do not carry it. `baseline` names the implementation every other one is compared with (see [paired comparisons](#paired-comparisons)); by default it is the first implementation that appears in each case. Blank lines are skipped. Each other line must be a JSON object, and its `artifact_version`, when present, must be the string `\"mmka_1\"`. Lines are interpreted by their `\"type\"`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:47
msgid "Required fields"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:49
msgid "`implementation` (string), `dataset_id`, `elapsed_us` (numbers)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:49
msgid "a timing of its case, unless `valid` is `false` or `batch_sink` is not `\"kept\"`; `phase`, `scale` (strings) and `block_id` (number) are read when present"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:50
#: manual/api/report.md:51
#: manual/api/report.md:52
#: manual/design/env_detect.md:160
#: manual/design/runner.md:246
#: manual/design/runner.md:247
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:50
msgid "counted in the capability matrix by `implementation` and `actual_kind` (`\"unclassified\"` when absent); a status of `invalid` or `infrastructure_failure` adds a mismatch row and, when `case` and `dataset_id` are present, removes that implementation's timings for that case and dataset"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:51
msgid "a counterexample row (minimal input, minimal fingerprint, shrink path, replay command)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:52
msgid "sets `run_id` and the corpus counts, and the protocol and seed of the comparisons when present; the last summary wins"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:53
msgid "anything else"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:53
msgid "ignored, including `calibration`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:55
msgid "The document has one `Scaling` plot per case, in order of first appearance, titled `\"Benchmark observations: <case>\"` (or `\"Benchmark observations\"` for observations without `case`), with unit `\"µs/op\"` and interval kind `\"median\"`. A plot contains only confirmatory timings: an observation whose `phase` is `\"confirmatory\"`, or that has no `phase` because it predates the field. Observations of any other phase are left out and counted in the plot's note. There is one point per implementation and scale: its x is the scale and its y the median `elapsed_us` of all confirmatory timings of that implementation at that scale, pooled over every dataset and repetition that shares the scale."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:66
msgid "Observations have"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:66
msgid "x value"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:68
msgid "the scale text"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:68
msgid "`Log` when positive finite values span at least 100x; otherwise `Linear` for finite numeric values or `Categorical`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:69
msgid "no `scale`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:69
msgid "the `dataset_id`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:69
msgid "as above"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:70
msgid "both kinds"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:70
msgid "the scale, or `dataset_id <n>`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:72
msgid "The note states what a point is and, when observations were left out, how many of which phase, for example `Excluded: 2 exploratory observations.` A case whose observations are all excluded keeps an empty plot, so that its note is shown. The corpus total is the sum of the four summary counts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:77
msgid "Errors are messages with the 1-based line number: invalid JSON, a line that is not an object, an unsupported or non-string artifact version, an observation without `implementation`, `dataset_id` or `elapsed_us`, a non-string `phase` or `scale`, a non-numeric `block_id`, a summary `protocol` that `@event.protocol_from_json` rejects (`invalid protocol at line <n>: <reason>`), and a summary `seed` that is not the decimal text of a `UInt64`. Without a line number: a `baseline` that names no implementation of the record, and a stream with neither observations nor mismatches nor counterexamples."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:107
#: manual/api/stats.md:102
msgid "Paired comparisons"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:109
msgid "`document_from_jsonl` also fills `PlotDocument.comparisons`: at every scale of every case, every implementation other than the baseline is compared with the baseline. A row is computed from the same confirmatory, valid, kept observations that the plot uses, in these steps."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:114
msgid "**Pairing.** Observations are paired by (case, scale, `block_id`). A block is complete when it holds exactly one observation of the baseline and one of the candidate; it gives the pair $(b_i, c_i)$ and the paired delta $d_i = c_i - b_i$. Every other block seen in either implementation is incomplete and counted in `blocks_incomplete`. Datasets that share a scale are pooled; the runner numbers blocks per scale, so their blocks never collide."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:121
msgid "**Failed validations.** A failing validation removes the implementation's observations of that case and dataset before pairing, also when it is a measurement validation (`EveryMeasurement`). The other implementation's blocks of that dataset are then incomplete, so a dataset on which either side failed never enters a decision."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:126
msgid "**Outliers.** The recorded `outlier_policy` is applied to the paired deltas with `@stats.filter_outliers`, never to either implementation's raw times. A pair is kept exactly when its delta is kept; the removed pairs are counted in `blocks_outliers`, and the kept ones in `blocks_used`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:130
msgid "**Enough blocks.** With fewer than 3 used blocks the row is `Unknown`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:131
msgid "**Decision.** `@stats.compare_paired_with_bootstrap` compares the used pairs with the recorded `practical_delta_pct`, 10000 resamples and 95 % confidence. The decision is that of the point estimate: with $r = 100\\,\\operatorname{med}(d)/\\operatorname{med}(b)$ and threshold $t$, `Faster` when $r \\le -t$, `Slower` when $r \\ge t$, `Equivalent` otherwise (an exact tie is `Equivalent` for every $t$). The interval is reported next to it and does not change it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:138
msgid "**Interval.** `DeltaInterval` holds the bootstrap interval of the median delta in µs/op and as a percentage of the baseline median, the scale of $r$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:142
msgid "Each row gets its own bootstrap seed: the 64-bit FNV-1a hash of the UTF-16 code units of"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:149
msgid "where `␟` is U+001F, the unit separator. The same record therefore gives the same intervals on every target, and the rows of a report get different seeds (up to a 64-bit hash collision), so adding a row does not change the interval of another."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:154
msgid "The settings come from the record's `summary`: `practical_delta_pct` and `outlier_policy` from its `protocol`, the run seed from its `seed`. A record without them (older records, hand-written streams) is compared with a 1 % threshold, `ReportOnly` and seed 0; `ComparisonReport.protocol_recorded` and `seed_recorded` are then `false`, and the note says that defaults were used. The confidence, the number of resamples and the minimum of 3 blocks are fixed by the report and named in the note."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:162
msgid "A row that cannot be decided says why in `reason`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:164
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:164
msgid "Reason"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:171
msgid "`bootstrap: <error>`, for example a paired delta that is not finite"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:173
msgid "Confirmatory observations without `block_id` cannot be paired; the note counts them."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/report.md:205
msgid "The paired deltas are $-3.0, -3.1, -3.0, -2.9$ µs/op up to rounding, their median is $-3.0$ and the baseline median $10.05$, so $r = 100 \\cdot (-3.0)/10.05 \\approx -29.85$, beyond the default threshold of $-1\\,\\%$: `Faster`. The seed shown is the FNV-1a hash of the row's key with run seed 42."
msgstr ""

