msgid "Imports"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:26
msgid "nothing"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:27
msgid "`model` (and `generator` also `moonbitlang/x/crypto`)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:35
msgid "Nothing imports `cli` or `env_detect`: the program that runs a benchmark calls `env_detect` and hands the snapshot to the runner, so the runner never probes the host. `stats` and `report` do not depend on `runner`, so they can analyse and render records produced elsewhere; `report` reads the recorded protocol through `event` and decides with `stats`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:41
msgid "Data flow"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:58
msgid "Everything before `run` is a description that is validated before it can run. Everything after `run` consumes preserved events. `run` is the only place where payloads execute and the timing clock is read. Processes are started by `runner` (subprocess workers), by `env_detect` (probing the host on native) and by `cli` (replay); files are read and written only by `env_detect` (`/proc/cpuinfo`) and `cli`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:65
msgid "Boundaries between packages"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:67
msgid "**Timing.** The timed region contains the payload and the output fold, plus setup only when the fixture's `SetupPolicy` includes it. Validation, warmup, calibration, event emission, the sink's `finish`, statistics and rendering are outside. The [runner design](design/runner.md) has the exact table."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:72
msgid "**Failure.** An operation's failure is a value (`ExecutionOutcome`), a validation's verdict is a value (`ValidationStatus`), and a failing validation emits a `ValidationFailure` with a minimized input and a replay command. A timeout or crash is infrastructure evidence, never a slow measurement."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:77
msgid "**Statistics.** Raw observations are never filtered or aggregated in the record. `stats` computes decisions from paired arrays; `OutlierPolicy` is applied only to derived values, and the report applies the recorded policy to paired deltas, never to stored observations."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:82
msgid "**Reports.** `report` is a pure projection. It plots and compares only confirmatory observations; invalid observations, discarded batches and the timings of implementations that failed validation on a dataset are excluded, and the failures are shown in the differential section. Its comparisons use the threshold, outlier policy and seed recorded in the run, or stated defaults for older records."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:89
msgid "**Tuning.** `tune` and `tune_gemm` hold policy and domain data. Building, validating and measuring candidates is done by the application with `runner`, so tuning measurements carry the same evidence as any other benchmark."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:93
msgid "Reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:95
msgid "A result is determined by five recorded inputs: the plan (case id, implementations and their versions, fixture id and version), the validated protocol, the run seed, the environment snapshot, and the code revision in the snapshot's provenance. The JSONL summary carries the protocol, the seed and the snapshot, and its `run_id` combines the case, the protocol identity, the seed and the provenance run id and timestamp, so every run is identified and can be re-analysed. Inputs are derived from the seed by [`generator`](design/generator.md), the implementation order is derived from the seed, and the bootstrap is seeded, so everything except the timings themselves is bit-reproducible on every target. Timings are comparable across runs when `environment_compatible` holds."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:107
msgid "Targets"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:109
msgid "All packages build on every target. `runner.run`, `execute_operation` and `env_detect.detect` are `async` and need the `moonbitlang/async` runtime (native, JS, wasm). Subprocess workers, `mare-mark replay` and stdin/stdout reports are native only; the non-native `cli` entry point supports file-to-file reports. `env_detect` probes the host on native and Node.js and reads environment variables elsewhere. Native and JS timings are different populations; compare them only as separately labelled runs."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:1
msgid "Repository conventions"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:3
msgid "These rules add to the Luna-Flow documentation standard for `mare_mark`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:5
msgid "Claims"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:7
msgid "Pages describe what the current branch implements. A capability is documented as available only when code and focused tests exercise it. Fields and enum cases that are recorded but not acted upon (for example `WorkspaceScope`) are documented as such, and every design page ends with the package's boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:13
msgid "Package pages"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:15
msgid "Every package, including the `cli` executable and the small `ir_sink` facade, has an API page, a tutorial and a design page. There is no separate package reference; the package table in the [overview](index.md) links all three pages of each package. `env_detect`, `report`, `runner` and `stats` also keep a short `README.mbt.md` beside their sources as a package-local pointer to the manual."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:22
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:24
msgid "Runnable examples are complete `test` or `async test` blocks that show their output with `inspect` or `debug_inspect`, and they are checked as described in [verification](verification.md). Examples never show machine-dependent values such as timings or decisions on real measurements."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:29
msgid "Units and names"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:31
msgid "Times are microseconds unless a page says otherwise, written `µs`. Relative deltas are percentages. Schema identifiers (`mmkp_2`, `mmka_1`, `mmks_2`, `mmkts_1`, and deprecated `mmkp_1`/`mmks_1`) are written exactly as they appear in artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:34
msgid "Translation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conventions.md:36
msgid "Commands, identifiers, package paths, schema names and version numbers stay unchanged in every translation."
msgstr ""

