#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:34
msgid "Detect the environment and hand its snapshot to the runner:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:61
msgid "`detect` filled in the target, the runtime, the CPU, the operating system, the host name, the time, the revision when it could find one, and a fresh run id. It cannot know how the code was compiled or how many operations the benchmark runs at once, so the test states both. The snapshot travels with the run: it is in the returned summary and in the `summary` line of a JSONL record."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:69
msgid "Say what the process cannot know"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:71
msgid "Four fields describe your build and your benchmark rather than the machine, and `detect` never guesses them:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:74
msgid "What to pass"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:76
msgid "how the code under test was built, for example `\"release\"` or `\"--release -O3\"`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:77
msgid "the numeric representation the results depend on, for example `\"f64\"` or `\"i64\"`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:78
msgid "the compiler version, unless `MARE_MARK_TOOLCHAIN` is set"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:79
msgid "how many operations the benchmark runs at once: `1` for the runner's sequential loop"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:81
msgid "These are semantic or performance fields, so `@model.environment_compatible` compares them: two runs built with different flags are not comparable, which is what you want."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:101
msgid "Pin a field"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:103
msgid "Any field can be overridden, detected or not. Pin the ones that must not change between the runs you want to compare, or that the probe gets wrong on your machine, for example a CPU name that differs between otherwise identical CI runners:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:123
msgid "Check what is missing before trusting a run"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:125
msgid "`undetected` lists every field that holds a fallback. Two runs whose `cpu` is `\"unknown\"` look compatible to `environment_compatible`, because `\"unknown\" == \"unknown\"`, so check the list before you compare runs or gate a release on them:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:147
msgid "The fields `target`, `gc`, `timestamp` and `run_id` always have a value; the others depend on the target and the host. On native and Node.js the CPU, the OS and the host name are usually found; in a browser and on wasm they come only from environment variables, if at all."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:152
msgid "Record the toolchain in CI"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:154
msgid "The compiler version is not visible to the running program. Set it in the environment of the test or benchmark job:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:162
msgid "`detect` reads `MARE_MARK_TOOLCHAIN` for `toolchain`. On GitHub Actions and GitLab CI the revision comes from `GITHUB_SHA` or `CI_COMMIT_SHA` without any setup; elsewhere set `GIT_COMMIT`, or let the native build ask `git rev-parse HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:167
msgid "Make a run id on its own"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:169
msgid "`new_run_id` is the generator `detect` uses for `run_id`. Call it when you build a snapshot by hand but still want a unique, time-ordered id:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:179
msgid "Pass `@env.now()` (from `moonbitlang/core/env`) as the argument to stamp the current time."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:184
msgid "**Hand-written snapshots still work.** The `@model` constructors remain the way to describe a machine you are not running on, or to write a fully deterministic test; see the [model tutorial](model.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:187
msgid "**The record keeps the snapshot.** A JSONL `summary` carries the `environment` object, so a report or a later comparison sees the same fields; see the [event API](../api/event.md#jsonl-records)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:190
msgid "**Run ids.** The runner's `RunSummary.run_id` includes the provenance `run_id` and `timestamp`, so a detected environment makes every run id unique; see the [model API](../api/model.md#run_identity)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:196
msgid "**Expecting the core count in `concurrency`.** It is in the `cpu` text. `concurrency` is the benchmark's own parallelism and stays `UNKNOWN_CONCURRENCY` (`0`) unless you pass it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:199
msgid "**Comparing runs with undetected fields.** `\"unknown\"` equals `\"unknown\"`; check `undetected` first."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:201
msgid "**Calling `detect` outside an async context.** It is an `async fn`; on wasm-gc there is no async runtime, so build the snapshot by hand there."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:203
msgid "**Expecting detected text to be stable across upgrades.** `runtime` includes the Node.js version and `cpu` the core count, so an upgraded runner image is a different performance environment. Pin the field if that is not what you want."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/env_detect.md:207
msgid "**Relying on `seq<n>` run ids across processes.** Without an entropy source the suffix is a per-process counter; two processes started in the same millisecond get the same id."
msgstr ""

